From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0918 redfin: the flash LED as a flashlight (PM8150L flash module)

New bsd/dev/sweet_torch.c: the PM8150L qpnp-flash-led-v2 module (SPMI SID 5,
0xd300), channels 0+1 (the rear LED, led:switch_2), torch mode with software
strobe and no safety timer, as leds-qpnp-flash-v2.c does it. sweettorch=1
looks only; =2 switches it (poke "t MA [MS]", sysctl kern.sweet_torch 0..1000);
=3 also blinks once at 5 mA. At most sweettorch_ma per channel (default 100,
cap 200; Android's torch is 300), at most sweettorch_secs (120, cap 600) at a
time, faults and over-temperature checked ten times a second while lit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WuzsiVGCDDmN2GPRLJvX3w
